1
00:06:11,428 --> 00:06:17,428
Imagine a place where nothing is impossible.

2
00:12:22,857 --> 00:12:28,857
Tomorrowland is a adventure, family, mystery film directed by Brad Bird.

3
00:18:34,285 --> 00:18:40,285
Bound by a shared destiny, a bright, optimistic teen bursting with scientific curiosity and a former boy-genius inventor jaded by disillusionment embark on a
danger-filled mission to unearth the secrets of an enigmatic place somewhere in time and space that exists in their collective memory as "Tomorrowland."

4
00:24:45,714 --> 00:24:51,714
Casey Newton, played by Britt Robertson.

5
00:30:57,142 --> 00:31:03,142
Frank Walker, played by George Clooney.

6
00:37:08,571 --> 00:37:14,571
Athena, played by Raffey Cassidy.

7
00:43:20,000 --> 00:43:26,000
David Nix, played by Hugh Laurie.

8
00:49:31,428 --> 00:49:37,428
Eddie Newton, played by Tim McGraw.

9
00:55:42,857 --> 00:55:48,857
Frank's Dad, played by Chris Bauer.

10
01:01:54,285 --> 01:02:00,285
Tomorrowland is a 2015 American science fiction film directed by Brad
Bird with a screenplay by Bird and Damon Lindelof.

11
01:08:05,714 --> 01:08:11,714
The film is based on the themed land Tomorrowland from the Disney
Parks and a story by Bird, Lindelof, and Jeff Jensen.

12
01:14:17,142 --> 01:14:23,142
It stars George Clooney, Hugh Laurie, Britt Robertson, Raffey
Cassidy, Tim McGraw, Kathryn Hahn, and Keegan-Michael Key.

13
01:20:28,571 --> 01:20:34,571
In the film, a disillusioned genius inventor and a teenage science enthusiast embark to an intriguing
alternate dimension known as "Tomorrowland", where their actions directly affect their own world.

14
01:26:40,000 --> 01:26:46,000
Walt Disney Pictures originally announced the film in June 2011 under the working title
1952 and later retitled it to Tomorrowland after the Disney Parks theme land.

15
01:32:51,428 --> 01:32:57,428
In drafting their story, Bird and Lindelof took inspiration from the progressive cultural movements of the Space Age, as well as Walt
Disney's optimistic philosophy of the future, notably his conceptual vision for the planned community known as EPCOT.

16
01:39:02,857 --> 01:39:08,857
Principal photography began in August 2013, with scenes
shot at multiple locales in five countries.

17
01:45:14,285 --> 01:45:20,285
Tomorrowland was released by Walt Disney Studios Motion Pictures
in conventional and IMAX formats on May 22, 2015.

18
01:51:25,714 --> 01:51:31,714
The film, which received mixed reviews from critics, grossed $209 million worldwide and was
considered a commercial failure for losing Disney $120–150 million at the box office.

19
01:57:37,142 --> 01:57:43,142
The film explores themes of inventor, apocalypse,
destiny, dreamer, futuristic car.

20
02:03:48,571 --> 02:03:54,571
The tone is uplifting and thought_provoking and mind_bending.
